Chapter: EffectLaunderFork
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (EffectRows.md stage 0). Fire-and-forget
 laundering: a def declared pure forks an effectful thunk and never
 awaits it. fork's parameter is a pure arrow (TypeEnv), so the
 thunk's Console effect is invisible to the spawner's signature.
 Effect rows stage 3b charges the spawner (fork : (Nothing -[e]-> a)
 -[e]-> Task a) and rejects this (CDX2090: the thunk's Console row
 cannot reconcile where the enclosing context requires purity).
 This test is the enforcement's regression guard.

Section: Definitions

  boom : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  boom (n) = act
    print-line-uni "boom"
    n
  end

  spawn-quiet : Integer -> Integer
  spawn-quiet (n) =
   let t = fork (\x -> boom 7)
   in n + 1

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (spawn-quiet 41))
  end
